ing to turn that  the issue of rising inflation in the u.s  how did joe biden go about reassuring  the american public  that while the economy is strong the  cost of living is going up right and  americans are not all convinced that the  economy is strong although there has  been good economic data since biden  became president  economy is just as much about how  someone feels in any kind of factual  numerical uh data you can see on a piece  of paper and that's something that biden  really tried to push home because the  economy is so important to winning  elections and so important to his  favorability rating as it is for any  president or any political leader really  and inflation has been very difficult  already before the russian innovation of  ukraine gas prices going up food prices  going up these kinds of things really  hitting the pocketbooks of average  americans and joe biden has to assure uh  americans that whatever action they take  against russia there will be a safety  net there so americans don't feel it and  i think we also have a clip of that of  something that joe biden was saying to  his  his voters  the panic also disrupted the global  supply chain  factories close  when that happens it takes longer to  make goods and get them to the  warehouses to the stores and go prices  go up  look at cars last year  one third of all the inflation was  because of automobile sales there  weren't enough semiconductors to make  all the cars that people wanted to buy  and guess what  prices of automobiles went way up  especially used vehicles as well but  and so we have a choice  one way to fight inflation is to drive  down wages and make americans poor  i think i have a better idea to fight  inflation  lower your cost not your wages  folks  that means make more cars than  semiconductors in america  more infrastructure and innovation in  america  more goods moving faster and cheaper in  america  more jobs where you can earn a good  living in america  instead of r